    <p>An <strong>engine</strong> converts the chemical energy of fuel into mechanical work. In an <strong>external combustion engine</strong> (such as a steam engine) fuel is burned outside the cylinder. In an <strong>internal combustion (IC) engine</strong>, fuel is burned <strong>inside the cylinder</strong>, and the hot expanding gases push a piston.</p>
