    <div style="background:#263238;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #ef5350;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <h3 style="color:#ffebee;margin-top:0;">🧠 Lesson Summary</h3>
    <p>Engine oil lubricates, cools, cleans, seals and protects. Lubrication systems include splash, pressure-fed, combined, petroil (two-strokes) and dry sump. A pressure system has a sump, strainer, pump, filter, relief valve, gallery and warning light. Viscosity grades (e.g. 15W-40) show oil thickness when cold and hot. Oil and filters must be changed at the recommended intervals and used oil recycled.</p>
    <h4 style="color:#ffebee;margin:16px 0 6px 0;">🗒️ Revision notes</h4>
    <ul style="margin:6px 0;padding-left:22px;">
    <li>Functions of oil.</li>
    <li>Lubrication systems.</li>
    <li>Pressure system parts.</li>
    <li>Oil grades.</li>
    <li>Filters and intervals.</li>
    </ul>
    </div>
